**Describe your issue**

Nesting a BEM --modifier/__element selector under a parent class with & produces a corrupted, non-matching selector in v4.3.3. Given:

```
@import 'tailwindcss';

  .header {
    &--transparent &__main {
      @apply border-transparent bg-transparent;
    }
  }
```

v4.3.2 compiles this correctly to:
```
.header {
    &--transparent &__main {
      border-color: transparent;
      background-color: transparent;
    }
  }
```

v4.3.3 compiles it to:
```
 :is(.header)--transparent :is(.header)__main {
    border-color: transparent;
    background-color: transparent;
  }
```

`:is(.header)--transparent` is not a valid/matching selector - the `--transparent` and `__main` BEM suffixes get split off the class name and appended after the :is() wrapper instead of staying attached to it, so the rule silently matches nothing.

This broke real usage in our project - a transparent header state, hover/focus-within variants, and a mega-menu visibility rule all stopped applying because their selectors no longer matched anything, with no build error or warning.

